WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.970
- There is concern the coming months

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.415
could create a twindemic.

00:00:04.415 --> 00:00:06.240
- COVID is continuing
to surge unfortunately.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.970
Doctors are now warning the flu

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.460
will also be a major threat

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.700
over the next few months.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.900
- When flu does come back,
and it will come back,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.830
it's gonna come back very aggressively.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:17.000
- [Narrator] Health experts are warning

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.530
that this year's flu
season could be much worse

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.660
than last year's.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.900
The CDC says from 9 million
to 45 million people

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.050
in the US get infected with
the flu annually leading

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.810
to 12,000 to 61,000 deaths.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.200
But that wasn't the case last year.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.130
Last year's flu season
was nearly nonexistent.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.470
Public health and clinical
laboratories reported

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.940
only a few thousand cases
of the flu for the season.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.920
The COVID pandemic is a big reason

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.980
why those numbers were so low.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.730
WSJ reporter, Felicia Schwartz,

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.840
has been reporting on
the upcoming flu season.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.550
- All of the experts and virologists

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.290
that I spoke to in the course

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.240
of reporting all of this out said

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:59.140
that there will definitely
be more flu than last year

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.660
and it could potentially be an earlier

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.480
and more severe season just as a result

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.320
of the weird dynamics last year.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.987
(pensive music)

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.590
- [Narrator] The flu virus
can spread to other people

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.850
through exposure, mainly
from droplets made

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.120
when people who have the
flu cough, sneeze or talk.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.930
Less often, a person might get the flu

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:24.080
from contact with surfaces
that have flu virus on it.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.770
And since the start of the pandemic,

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.010
health experts have found COVID spreads

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.480
in much the same way.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.920
During last year's flu season

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.150
with the roll out of COVID
vaccines just getting started,

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.130
much of the US was in lockdown.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.320
Social distancing
guidelines were in effect

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.420
and many people were masked.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.660
All things that help
prevent the spread of COVID

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.020
and also help prevent the flu.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.700
Now COVID vaccines are widely available

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.520
and people are interacting more.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:54.270
- People are back at school,
back at work to some extent.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.660
Depending on where you live in the US,

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.080
there are or aren't social
distancing restrictions,

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:03.500
like mask wearing and congregating

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.290
in large groups and so on.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:08.610
And so there is a lot more
opportunity for the flu

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.790
to spread this year.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:11.750
- [Narrator] As a population,

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.530
there's also less immunity
to the flu this year.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:15.900
Population immunity occurs

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.210
when people are naturally
infected by the virus

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.820
or have received a vaccine.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.310
Since so few people were
infected with the flu last year

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.635
because of social distancing,

00:02:23.635 --> 00:02:25.550
people haven't been able to build up

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.510
their natural immune defenses.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.590
This lack of immunity could contribute

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.820
to what some health experts
are calling a twindemic.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.300
It refers to the threat
of a severe flu outbreak

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.491
on top of the COVID-19 pandemic,

00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:40.905
which could be detrimental
to the healthcare system.

00:02:40.905 --> 00:02:43.572
(pensive music)

00:02:45.376 --> 00:02:47.570
- And I think the fear
from health authorities

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:50.340
is that hospitals could
be further overwhelmed.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.310
One hospital administrator was telling me

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.740
maybe they'd have to
cut back on clinic hours

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.090
or reschedule other procedures

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:59.080
if they've having to make
these kinds of choices.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.230
They might have to scale some things back.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.380
- [Narrator] This overlap
could also cause confusion

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:06.170
among people above
whether they have COVID-19

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.140
or the flu.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.570
Because they have similar symptoms,

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:11.430
it could be hard to diagnose
which condition people have

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.120
based on the symptoms alone.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.410
The main difference between the two

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:16.680
is that COVID symptoms typically appear

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.730
about five days after infection

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:22.390
but symptoms can appear 2
to 14 days after infection.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.150
And flu symptoms usually appear

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.803
about one to four days after infection.

00:03:26.803 --> 00:03:29.470
(pensive music)

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.570
The good news is the best ways

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.760
to prevent catching the flu

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.760
are the ones many people
are already familiar with.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.550
- Infectious disease experts

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.760
and epidemiologists really urge you

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.400
to get a flu shot.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.160
On top of that, hand
washing, good hygiene.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.670
If you're already wearing masks

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.110
and practicing social
distancing for corona,

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:52.330
that definitely can't hurt you

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.260
if you're looking to
avoid catching the flu.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.820
- [Narrator] The flu season
commonly strikes the US October

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:01.290
through May with cases peaking
in December through February.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.120
So the CDC recommends
getting a flu shot every year

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.363
by the end of October to get ahead of it.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.430
(pensive music)

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.680
The CDC says you can get both the flu shot

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.890
and the COVID vaccine,

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.200
including boosters at the same time,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.290
which wasn't the guidance last year.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.471
- The shots were so new,

00:04:19.471 --> 00:04:21.120
they didn't really have enough information

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.070
to make their recommendation

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:24.650
but now they're saying yes,
you can go get those two shots

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:25.540
at the same time.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.337
So depending also on the booster campaign,

00:04:27.337 --> 00:04:30.790
maybe there'll be some more
co-administration of shots.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.290
- [Narrator] As far as side effects

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.870
from taking both the COVID
vaccine and the flu shot

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:36.000
at the same time,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.450
the CDC says the side
effects people experience

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.840
are similar to what they experience

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.930
when the vaccines are given separately.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.390
Some pharmaceutical companies

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:45.210
are even working on a combined flu shot

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.200
and COVID vaccine that
could be administered

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.480
in the same jab.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.930
But there's no clear timeline yet

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.720
on when those would be available.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.580
While experts believe this flu season

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.300
could strike earlier and
more severely than usual,

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.470
there's still no guarantee it will be.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.190
- One person I interviewed
described it to me

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.393
as a tricky devil.

00:05:01.393 --> 00:05:03.350
It's very hard to predict.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:05.790
So I think there's a general feeling

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.420
that it will be worse,

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.440
and some people think it could be very bad

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:13.070
but it's kind of hard
to know at this point.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.230
If you're worried about the flu,

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.150
probably the single
best thing you could do

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.937
is go out and take a shot.

00:05:17.937 --> 00:05:20.604
(pensive music)

